Layout: FLAT -- all headers and sources in this one directory, so a single
include path (-Ivendor/weirdike) resolves every bare #include.

Contents = upstream include/ + src/core/ + src/esp/ + src/crypto/.

ALSO vendored (AP1, 2026-09-26): src/transport/udp_bsd.* -- upstream's POSIX
transport, byte-identical from the pinned commit. The DAEMON still does not
use it, on purpose: udp_bsd owns its socket and offers a blocking recv();
weirdiked needs the opposite -- it polls the sockets itself together with
the TUN fd and the control socket, demultiplexes UDP-4500 with
natt_classify() and feeds only the IKE datagrams to
weirdike_input_datagram(). Its transport vtable therefore has a send() and
a recv() that always reports "nothing" -- the same split the ESP32
integration uses. udp_bsd is here for the host lifecycle test and for any
future consumer that wants the blocking upstream shape.

  examples/, tests/         Host-only.

